    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«たとたん» expresses that something happened just at the moment another action ended.",
     "texto": [
      "It usually introduces an unexpected or uncontrolled result. It isn't normally used for a voluntary, planned action by the speaker.",
      "ドア を 開けた とたん、強い 風 が 入って きました。 (As soon as I opened the door, a strong wind came in.)",
      "電気 が 消えた とたん、部屋 は 真っ暗 に なりました。 (As soon as the light went out, the room became pitch dark.)"
     ],
